solution has they call them base stations and it&nbsp;
receives a signal they all operate this similar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:08.080
they receive a signal to the camera tracker&nbsp;
and that camera tracker gets tied in unison&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:13.960
with a in-game camera so there's an actual camera&nbsp;
inside Unreal Engine we call a c camera actor and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:20.520
that's through a a plugin in Unreal Engine ties&nbsp;
both of those in unison so the camera tracker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:26.560
and the in-game camera so when it's tied together&nbsp;
basically when you move your camera tracker on top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:32.800
